From a6aa4d85a985c546a2b65caf868ec80c8591b2da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccr <ccr@aciceri.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:51:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] voice: tap decoded live output and make local playback
 optional

LivePeerCore always opened the default speaker and rendered the remote
Opus track to it, so a live call could only exist on the machine holding
the audio devices.

Add LiveCallbacks::output, which receives each decoded frame as mono f32
at 48 kHz, and a local_playback flag that skips PlaybackStream entirely.
The three duplicated write_output/level.observe pairs in
receive_output_audio collapse into one emit_output helper that feeds the
speaker, the tap and the RMS level window.

The level callback is unaffected by the flag: it was already computed
separately from playback.

(cherry picked from commit 19005d0a8c772ccba24e294092ccd3ff58bf271b)
